From 4994c7571db5e105862107defa917f59d5679f62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arc-moe <arc-moe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:18:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] sycl: device code without FP64 for Arc A-series
 (Alchemist)

Xe-HPG (DG2: A770/A750/A580/A380) has no FP64 unit. Eight kernel files
accumulate in double (router top-10 softmax, GDN/QSA RMS norms, shared expert
gate, moe_combine, PLE, sampler nucleus, quantize_q8_0, silu): an AOT build for
acm-g10 stops with "Double type is not supported on this platform" and a JIT
build fails at the kernel's first launch.

- strata/sycl_fp.hpp: sfp_t is float under STRATA_SYCL_NO_FP64, double
  otherwise (Battlemage keeps upstream's arithmetic bit for bit).
- Those device functions use sfp_t, sfp_t(...) literals, sfp_t local arrays
  and sizeof(sfp_t) for their dynamic local memory.
- CMake: STRATA_SYCL_NO_FP64 defaults to ON when STRATA_SYCL_AOT names an
  Alchemist part (acm-*, dg2).
- CMake: -ze-opt-greater-than-4GB-buffer-required for every kernel (the
  expert cache is one 10-15 GB allocation), and STRATA_SYCL_IGC_EXTRA for
  further IGC options; both reach ocloc (AOT) and the JIT.
---
